        "updated_at": "2026-04-08T22:37:49Z",
        "body": "Closing this PR — the updates it proposed have already been incorporated (and expanded on) in main.\n\n## What happened\n\nThis branch was opened on March 7 to refresh the org README: fix branding (diVine → Divine), update the repo map, and note the `divine-cdn-worker` deprecation. Since then, commit 7863ea9 on main landed a more comprehensive version of the same overhaul.\n\n## Why not merge\n\nMerging this PR would actually regress the README. The current main version includes:\n\n- **~30 repos** with tech stacks, deployment URLs, and descriptions (vs. ~15 in this PR with no stacks)\n- **Full architecture tables** organized by category (Frontend, Core Backend, Trust & Safety, Edge & Infra, Libraries & SDKs)\n- **Detailed \"How It Works\" sections** covering Nostr protocol, Blossom media storage, C2PA Content Credentials, and Keycast authentication (vs. a 4-bullet summary)\n- **Development setup instructions** for web, mobile, and Rust services\n- **Repos this PR drops entirely**: divine-space, divine-inquisitor, divine-relay-sync, funnel, divine-realness, social-media-age-rules-db, divine-name-sync, divine-identify-verification-service, divine-github-actions, keycast_flutter_demo, c2pa-flutter, c2pa-rs, media-kit, divine-resurrection, brand-guidelines\n\nThe PR also has merge conflicts with the current main branch, which would need to be resolved before merging regardless.\n\n## One thing worth keeping\n\nThe explicit deprecation note for `divine-cdn-worker` → `divine-blossom` is not currently called out on main. If that's still relevant, it could be added as a small follow-up.",
